From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:06:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize the end of a list element before it is read

SplitStringListInternal() declares the end position of each list
element without a value. ValueStateTransition() sets it on every path
that sets the start position, and it is read only once a start position
is set, but GCC 10 and 12 do not see through the transition and
-Wmaybe-uninitialized reports the read. The end position starts out as
zero, which the transition replaces before any read.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/function/cast/vector_cast_helpers.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/function/cast/vector_cast_helpers.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/function/cast/vector_cast_helpers.cpp
index 579b6db8dc..0a5f4a85d3 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/function/cast/vector_cast_helpers.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/function/cast/vector_cast_helpers.cpp
@@ -288,7 +288,7 @@ static bool SplitStringListInternal(const string_t &input, OP &state) {
 	bool seen_value = false;
 	while (pos < len) {
 		optional_idx start_pos;
-		idx_t end_pos;
+		idx_t end_pos = 0;
 
 		while (pos < len && (buf[pos] != ',' && buf[pos] != ']')) {
 			if (!ValueStateTransition(input_state, start_pos, end_pos)) {
